SlotObject: set ordinary slots directly; explicit constructors for Dependency and _dep_choice

SlotObject.__init__ probed every slot with getattr() before setting it.
For a class whose slots are all ordinary (named once, no property or class
attribute in front of them; checked once per class) the probe of a new
instance is always negative, so the slots are now set directly, in the
same order. Dependency and _dep_choice, which the resolver creates by the
hundred thousand, get explicit keyword constructors that make the same
assignments; subclasses and unknown keywords go through the generic
constructor as before.

On top of patches 0001-0016, resolve seconds before -> after
(median of the runs, at least 2 per figure):
  start 32.3 -> 30.0, holds 16.0 -> 15.1, masks 34.7 -> 32.0,
  py313 19.4 -> 18.4, bdeps 23.2 -> 21.9, policykit 16.5 -> 15.3
  sum of six 142.1 -> 132.7 (-9.5 s, -2.1 % of the stock sum 447.5)
Patches 0001-0017 together: 447.5 -> 132.7 s (-70 %); 447.5 is the
stock sum of the ladder run of 2026-11-20, stock was not run again here.

Weak spots and what was not checked:
* One documented difference: a slot given a non-None value before the
  constructor ran and not passed as a keyword is set to None where the old
  loop raised AssertionError.

Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in the emerge-fast job, 2026-11-17..20;
isolated from the full patch and measured on 2026-11-20..21. Not a human-written
change. Base: Portage 3.0.83. Test: `emerge -p -uND @world` on six states of
one system image, one resolve at a time; every run gave the same merge list
in the same order, the same number of backtracking attempts and the same
package count as unpatched 3.0.83.
